.TH BINGUX-CALCULATOR 1 "2026-11-09" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-calculator \- calculator for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-calculator
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-calculator
opens the Calculator window with four modes: Basic, Scientific, Programmer
and Convert.
Type on the keyboard or press the keys.
The result shows as you type, and Enter finishes the calculation and adds it
to the history.
.PP
Arithmetic is exact: 0.1 + 0.2 is 0.3, and 100! shows all of its digits.
A result with no exact value, such as the square root of 2, shows to 16
significant digits; the Precision menu sets 10 to 50.
.PP
Only one Calculator window runs.
A second launch raises the window that is open.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B Basic
The four operations, percent as in a till (200 + 10% is 220), and the answer
carried on: after Enter, an operator continues from the result.
.TP
.B Scientific
Brackets, powers, roots, logarithms, trigonometry in degrees or radians
(an inverse set under 2nd), hyperbolic functions, factorials, constants and a
memory (mc, m+, m\-, mr).
.TP
.B Programmer
Whole numbers of 8, 16, 32 or 64 bits, signed or unsigned, in binary, octal,
decimal and hexadecimal at once, with a grid of bits to flip.
Results wrap to the word size, as they do in hardware.
.TP
.B Convert
Length, mass, temperature, volume, area, speed, time, data, energy, power,
pressure, angle, fuel economy and currency.
The expression field in Basic and Scientific also converts: type
.B 5 km to miles .
.SH CURRENCY
Rates are the European Central Bank's daily reference rates, downloaded once
a half day and kept in the cache.
Without a network the last download is used, or the rates built into the
program, and the window says which.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Enter
Finish the calculation.
.TP
.B Escape
Clear the entry; again, clear the answer.
.TP
.B Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+4
Switch mode.
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
Show or hide the history.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the result.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/bingux-calculator/state.json
The history, the mode and the settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/bingux-calculator/rates.json
The exchange rates last downloaded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-files (1),
.BR bingux\-settings (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/calculator.md in the Bingux source.
